WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome back to the show, everybody.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:06.100
The Super Bowl was last night, and now Tariq and I both have

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.100
a bunch of leftovers that we don't want to waste,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.000
so we've challenged each other to come up with the best dish

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.100
using only Super Bowl leftovers.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.167
It's time for the "Super Bowl Leftovers Challenge."

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:20.000
-♪ Super Bowl Leftovers Challenge, yeah ♪

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.167
-Whoever makes the most delicious dish

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:26.367
gets to take home the Golden Buffalo Wing.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.434
Tariq, what would this honor mean to you?

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.033
-Absolutely nothing, Jimmy.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.767
-Now, we are not doing this alone.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:37.367
We're each getting help from an amazing New York City chef.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.133
He's the host of "Cook at All Costs" on Netflix

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:43.901
and the owner of the Filipino taquerias Flip Sigi.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.667
His new restaurant, Carriage House,

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:46.934
opens this spring.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:50.267
Please welcome Chef Jordan Andino.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.033
Chef Jordan Andino. Good to see you, bud.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.167
-What up, what up? -Thank you, Chef. Alright.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.868
-Let's go! -Here's how this works.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:03.701
We have to use at least three of these leftovers

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:05.801
and make something good out of it, okay?

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.901
And as soon as we hear this sound...

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.667
[ Rasta horn blares ]

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.601
...that means it's a dance party.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.968
No, that means we have a minute left.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:17.033
So, once we're done, our dishes will be judged by Questlove.

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:20.067
We have placed him in an isolation room.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.200
Quest, please put on the dome of silence

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.767
so that you can neither see or hear anything.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.033
It's right there.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.200
Jordan, any advice before we start?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.234
-Oh, yeah, I was having a little convo here. Yes.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.400
-That doesn't seem fair.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.634
But whatever. Wow. That's the way we're gonna play it, huh?

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:41.834
-A little advice. Take your time, have fun with it,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.167
and keep in mind I'm going to be there to help both of y'all.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.901
-Both of us? -Yeah, I'm going to be jumping

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.167
back and forth.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.334
-You seem pretty chatty with Tariq already.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:51.300
Wait. How come mine says "Jimmy"?

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.300
What does yours say? -GOAT. GOAT, Jimmy.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.701
-Wait. I have one, too. I have one, too. Wait.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.834
Mine -- I just want to get ready with you guys.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.434
-Yeah, of course. You have an apron. Good.

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:00.634
-Yeah. We're ready. -Okay.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.067
-Does it say something? -No, no.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.801
Mine just is blue. I'm just ready to --

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.601
Ready to go. -Alright. Alright.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:09.100
Don't set us up for something that doesn't pay off.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.067
-Oh, sorry, sorry, sorry. -Alright. Here we go.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.100
On the count of "three," let's start cooking.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.868
One, two, three. What are you grabbing?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.067
-Go, go, go.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.300
-Alright. I'm gonna go -- -What are you doing?

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.067
-Come on. -Chef, help me out.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.567
-Okay. Go. -I have an idea.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.100
I want to make tater tots on that waffle iron.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.734
-Okay. Genius. -And make a tater-tot waffle.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:31.234
-That's amazing. -Does that sound good?

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.300
-Oil both sides. -So what do we put on that?

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.534
I was thinking chicken tenders. -Chicken tenders?

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.501
But that's, like, fried on fried.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.267
So something bright. Something bright.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.133
-Something bright? -Right. Like, some of this.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.367
-Pizza? Cheese? -Some of the guac.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.934
-[ Muttering ] No chicken at all.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.100
Help Tariq out. He's making chips.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.601
Chips and dip for Tariq.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:52.567
-Yeah, I'm just gonna -- Excuse me.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:56.334
-What -- Are you eating? You got to be making stuff.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.567
You're not at my party, dude.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.334
We're not at the party. Oh, maybe -- How about chili?

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:03.767
Should I put chili and cheese on it?

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:05.501
-Chili would be good. Chili would be good.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.167
Oh, actually, I guess the tenders.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:08.667
The tenders with the sauce?

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.501
-Wait. Tenders -- -Fried chicken and waffles?

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.701
Chicken and waffles. -If I cut the chicken tenders?

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.000
-Yeah, yeah, make a sauce. Make a sauce. Here, here.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.734
-What do you mean, make a sauce?

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:18.634
-Make a sauce. Make a sauce. -With the chicken tenders?!

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.067
-Make a sauce.

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.968
-Stop yelling "make a sauce" at me!

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.334
[ Rasta horn blares ]

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.033
-Ohh! -Oh, that's a minute.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.501
Don't cut yourself. There you go. Put it in. Okay.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.601
-What is Tariq doing? He's just eating!

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.934
This is ridiculous.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.000
-You have to taste it. You have to taste it.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.634
-How's it taste? -That's good.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:37.033
-I kept it simple, man. What you got going over here?

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.734
-Don't worry about what's going down over here, man!

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.067
-Ready, ready, ready? -Yes. What do I do?

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.033
-It's a little hot. It's hot.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.300
-Alright. What do we do?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.801
[ Laughter ] -Go under, go under.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.000
♪♪

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.334
-Alright. Chef, thank you so much for your help.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:59.267
-Toss it, toss it, toss it, toss it.

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.534
-Alright.

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.267
Alright. Here we go. Alright. Good.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.601
-Na-cheese-mo. -Na-cheese-mo.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.167
-What did you do? What --

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.434
-It's -- Okay.

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:15.868
I layered up the seven-layer dip,

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.868
the artichoke dip, a little guac on the side.

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.968
-Yeah, amazing. I don't know how you thought of this.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.667
Putting stuff on top.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.934
You're a real culinary genius. Alright.

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.767
Tariq, do you want dish one or dish two?

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.801
-Dish one. One, obviously.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.801
-No. I'll do dish two, man. -Thank you.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.067
The GOAT spot.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.701
-Is it now time?

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:39.000
Quest may now exit the isolation room.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.334
Can you take the dome --

00:04:40.334 --> 00:04:42.067
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.167
-Yes. Take it off. Yes. This is --

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.567
I don't want you falling.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.801
It's me. It's me. It's me.

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.934
Alright. Dude, sorry. Alright. Here you go.

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:53.167
You're right there. Quest.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:55.434
Questlove. Welcome back to the show, by the way.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.634
Great job on all the stuff

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:58.300
you've done in your whole career.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.567
What a great career.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.400
Chef, do you want to explain what the first one is

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.734
and what the second one is?

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:07.901
-Yeah, so, the first dish, dish one, is Na-cheese-mo.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:12.300
It's, like, 12 layers of nachos and chips and deliciousness.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.634
-Okay.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.200
-How'd we do? Yeah.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.934
Uh, dish two...

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:25.601
-What? -Dish two is a tater-tot waffle.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.267
It's, like, fried chicken and waffles,

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.434
so tater-tot waffle with Sriracha honey.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:32.067
-This is a waffle? -Yeah.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.501
-Okay. Where do I start?

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.801
-Start with the chips and guac.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:40.234
-I don't trust that.

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:41.467
I'm gonna start with this first.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.334
-Ooh. Okay.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:50.634
♪♪

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.434
Ooh, honey and Sriracha.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:54.634
♪♪

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.734
Whoever did this is an immaculate artist

00:05:56.734 --> 00:06:01.133
because even the presentation is, like, on point.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:04.167
-Yeah, it's like a Picasso over there.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.701
-No, no.

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:08.200
-What does it taste like? Chips and dip?

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.968
-I think I'm ready to make my decision.

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:14.601
-Alright. We're ready for the decision.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:16.601
Quest, please write down. Very important.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:19.400
Who won the Golden Wing?

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.434
Write it down and make sure you put it in the ballot box.

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.934
This is a decision --

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.334
I'm shaking. Alright. -Alright.

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:27.767
-Now that you've put it in the box,

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:29.267
Quest, can you take it out of the box?

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:31.100
-Now I got to take it out of the box?

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:35.300
-And reveal -- reveal --

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.767
I just want to make sure there's no tampering!

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:40.434
No tampering. Take it out of the box.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:42.734
-I could have just easily told you which one I like better.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:44.400
-It doesn't matter. It doesn't matter.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.467
Now we know -- Now we know that no one tampered with the result.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:49.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:55.801
-The winner of the Super Bowl Leftover Challenge is...

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.200
I like dish one.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.000
-Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.868
-One. One.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:02.033
-Come on, man.

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:04.534
-A tater-tot waffle?

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:08.501
-Philly! Philly! This is for you!

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:11.767
E-A-G-L-E-S!

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.434
Eagles!

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:17.167
-Congratulations to the Super Bowl Leftovers Challenge

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:18.834
winner, Tariq Trotter. -♪ Fly, Eagles, fly ♪

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.968
-Thanks again to Chef Jordan Andino. Stick around.

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:23.300
We'll be right back with more "Tonight Show," everybody.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:25.634
-We did it, baby! We did it! I'm taking this one home!

